   129	They were good finals. The Current girl went out in the Iron semifinal to a Blade from the lake house, on figures, after four level exchanges, and came off the floor with her chin up. The house's bench cheered her. Most of the north benches were polite. A woman Lira had signed a card for on the first morning, before any of it, caught her eye across the square during the Copper final and smiled at her, quickly, and then looked away as if she had been caught at something.
   130	
   131	Lira found she did not mind as much as she had at the rope yesterday. *A town remembering what its licences cost.* She could understand that. She had been a town like that herself, once, at a station counter, with her form in her hand.
