   189	Nothing did. At the ferry the two grey coats were on the landing in their usual places, under the rain, as if it were not raining. One of them watched the program wagon go aboard behind the coach, with the colors trunk lashed on top of it, and did not look at the coach at all.
   190	
   191	*Lira, the confluence, the Silver Rank Eight: two touches to one, on the fourth. Twenty-seven to twenty-eight. Six bursts, one of them borrowed. She asked me to watch her feet and tell her first, and I did, and I'll keep doing it as long as she asks. The floor had four facts on it and I found three. Rooke wrote the fourth as his. It was mine as much as his. I looked at that corner too.*
   192	
   193	*The order: one sentence, served at the hour it would be seen. Fifty-one seconds there and fifty-one back. A woman with a baby on her shoulder asked who thanks a man for that. The hall went on liking us and stopped saying so, which is worse, because there's nothing to answer.*
   194	
   195	He looked at the last line for a while. Then he wrote one more under it.
   196	
   197	*Nothing in the order was wrong. They chose the hour.*

