    14	
    15	Seln was not on the bench. He was up in the little loft over the west doors, where the stewards kept their spare benches, at its corner. Cael had seen him go up there before the hall filled. From that corner a man could see the whole square, and every door in the hall, and every face on both sets of benches, without turning his head.
    16	
    17	At the east end of the square, on the quiet side, the Stone stood by himself at the end of the panel's table with his arms folded.
    18	
