    41	She spent her burst then. It was the only one Rooke had given her for the exchange, and she spent it to find the bottom. She went off her back foot low and short, sideways along the top course's edge, and came down on the far side of it with her whole weight on one leg, and he saw her knee give a little as she landed. Not with pain. With surprise. The floor under her was deeper than her leg had been told.
    42	
    43	And while she was finding that out, the Silver had taken the centre.
    44	
