editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-520-**Prose vs plan differences.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-521-- (a) The first sitting is the **sixth** Fifth-day (day 40), not "the fourth Fifth-day of the month", so that the trial, the envelopes (two nights), the budget and the four frames evenings fit in order before it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-522-- (b) The month's close is written on day 42 (two nights after the sitting).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-523-- (c) Seln's index is delivered in ch8 as the sheaf, and he is given the ch10 coach joke and a ch9 counter scene (both new).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-524-- (d) The honest floor of ch11 (lanes as a builder's courses) is new; it prepares the trial.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-525-- (e) The house's escort is the head groom, his son and Bracken's senior clerk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-526-- (f) Havel's cutaway runs ~1,240 words against the packet's ~1.5k.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-527-- (g) "They've filed the face out of it" is in Cael's log, not spoken.
