editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-529-## New canon minted (flag where marked)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-530-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-531-- **The annex (flag):** the old lumber room across the library's top landing, cleared on Bracken's order on day 9 for the assistant's table and a shelf for the code; the house calls the pair of rooms "the annex".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-532-- **Seln's sheaf (flag):** a forty-leaf taped cross-index of the instrument (paragraph → sections → each section's history), pushed under the reading-room door before dawn on day 9; the wing's register "has no sheaf in it". The second volume's own index runs eleven years behind the volume.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:533:- **The nine days (flag):** the first renewal's minute (Halcenvane, the inspection year) was *held for countersignature* by the inspection delegation's officer and sealed nine days after the panel sat; the house's enrollment book carries the panel day; the sealed minute went to the registry file; only Cael's old Log holds both days. The rebuilt table gives sitting and seal days for all three rows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-534-- **The ninety-one (flag):** recorded invocations of the integrity provisions: eighty-four about things; seven about persons, every one about conduct; **line sixty-three is Bracken's fourth-year filing** (spelt *cassing*, kept with *(sic)* at his request).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-535-- **Bracken's black oilcloth ledger** of the weight of every answer the house has filed in his time; the post-room's brass parcel beam.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-536-- **The house's escort** (head groom, his son, the senior clerk of nine years on the enrollment book).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-537-- **The seat's notice text** (ch10) and *per seal* (a code section for proceedings the registry designates institutional; never used in Bracken's thirteen years).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-538-- **Jent (flag — appearance):** middle height and years, brown coat with cuffs mended in another brown, spectacles on a black cord, a screw-lid travelling inkwell; addresses Cael as "Hesk-ward".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-539-- **The house's exhibit list:** 173 items on eleven pages; Jent's nine (listed in ch10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-540-- **The wool exchange:** four steps on a plinth; lanolin; lot numbers carved in the selling floor; a side door newly cut; the conference room was the wool-factors' counting room; five evaluation chairs under grey covers; the seat's seal device "the river and the scale".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-541-- **The board line** *The house will attend.* (Bracken's).
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-545-- **The Force third-year (flag — style):** builds Force into the floor in courses on a settle in the knees, on his own count (four, then two when building fast); a fan; a well of four courses; laughs when surprised.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-546-- **The lane's slope (flag):** three lanes close together cost ten, ten, twelve counts; untested past three. Consistent with the accepted "ten counts slow" limit; it adds that the bill grows with close spending.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-547-- **Lira's correction:** lie with the foot you don't care about; go on the fourth against a builder.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-548-- **The district's confirmation text** with *outcome anticipated: advancement, per title*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-549-- **The side-door officer:** young, a heavy cold, a ruled board; the door log's two columns (name; standing).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-550-- **Havel at Ostrand:** the inn by the bridge; junior chair, rotation "the seat's Fifth-days, until relieved"; the senior chair district grade; the five sheets stay at the inn on sitting days; "told, once, in a room with the door shut, that the mark was not his clearance".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-551-- **Withrow:** the charter folder in the locked case under the framed charter, key on her chain; the two old adverse notes (a fire-watch quarter; a year's declarations unindexed) with remedies and clearances.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-552-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:553:**Coordinator correction (2026-10-10).** Seln learns why Shadow was sealed in SOURCE Ch15 (The Cache), which is the edition's MOVEMENT 6 (BOOK_MAP §3 item 15, §6, §9) — not in M3. Until M6 he does not know a sealed thing exists.
