editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:651:- **Vastin's room (flag, minor):** the porter feeds the pigeons from the same half-circle; a **letter-book** of fair copies of everything that left the room in nineteen years; the lowest drawer at the far end of the cabinet of shallow drawers holds what is his; the floor's lamps go out at the half-bell after six (the house's rule); the candle on the consumables under his name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:652:- **Vastin's clerk (flag):** nine years in the outer office; narrow, tidy; his one non-work sentence ("Will you be getting home tonight, sir? It's set in to rain.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:653:- **Vastin's two chapter-fourteen files (flag):** a hill station keeper whose cracked housing read every Ash a rank high for six years, covered by false returns; a coastal district officer paid to enter a rank no frame had read; the second's daughter's letter answered *no*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:654:- **Vastin's four supplementary findings (flag):** a district's enrollment challenge (decisive against the district, which wrote without grievance), a hill station's frame (retired on his evidence), a guild hall's matter, a sponsorship quarrel — all received.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-655-- **The two provisions (flag):** an evaluator who has examined the subject may lay his finding before proceedings (the old one: *shall receive*); nine recorded uses, all received (Karis's count from the digest).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:656:- **The northern junior's file (flag — plant):** a young evaluator from the northern district; a station Kindling entry four years old for a young woman whose shown work runs ahead of it, within tolerance; *continue observation*; Vastin keeps the copy in *held*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-657-- **Withrow (flag):** "form thirty, refusals, third series" in the registry's second-year drafting book; she taught it as a mercy to every junior; her haulier: Force, Bronze Rank Four, thirty-one, guild haulage contract in a river district, wife, son and daughter, fourteen years owing; a station clerk's slip twenty years before; two silent frames; seven weeks; nine letters from four offices brought in a flour sack on the fourth day; east past the last station in eighteen months; the daughter is M1's daughter at the counter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-658-- **The counsel (flag):** she heard the refusal at the long low inn on the wharf where the seat's clerks eat on sitting weeks; refused without citation "perhaps five times" in twenty-six years; turns her steel rule a quarter turn at the end of each part of an argument.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-659-- **Bracken's post procedure (flag):** a second trestle; four chalked boards *HOUSES. SPONSORS. FACULTIES. OTHER.*; the daily count in his counter daybook; heaviest day 196; fourteen chartered houses answered in the same two lines (text in ch16); grey-sealed seat letters carried up by hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-660-- **The gatepost board (flag):** *The house has answered the challenge in its filing. The filing is public. The house has nothing to add to it.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-661-- **Rooke:** business in the town on Third-day evenings; the sentence to the correspondent; the program floor closed to observers from day 46 (shutters, chain and padlock, card *PROGRAM FLOOR CLOSED TO OBSERVERS. BY ORDER.*), the visitors' ledger kept with *none*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-662-- **The visitors' log (flag):** the program clerk's second ledger from shortly after the first sitting; twenty-six names in a fortnight; four from outside houses (two Rhagen, the lake house, a northern house).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-663-- **Wing three's gallery (flag):** a narrow timber gallery over the west door from when wing three was the house's examination room, used to store benches until the porters cleared it for the four observers; observers enter by the lodge book.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-664-- **The Current third-year (flag — style):** Iron Rank Four, tall, glides "the way water goes over a weir"; two glides and a bend; adapts to straight glides, then glide-and-step.
--
