editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-153-**Bodies.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-154-- **Cael:** fit. Rested the hip on d30 by Rooke's order, after four bursts on the second floor's boards (worth five there). A stung left forearm from Ephram's lath (d29), a day's matter. The right shoulder is unused. Shadow rent runs from waking; drifts are in the gaps only; one in the last recess week. Zero deployment anywhere.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-155-- **Lira, Brom, Ephram:** fit. Ordinary floor knocks from the mock bouts. Brom's right fist is strapped from habit, healed.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-158-**Fragments and progression.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-159-- Six confirmed plus the anomaly (uncounted). No new capability, and no public record changes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-160-- In the mock bout Cael used only the public suite at documented rates (Wind bursts and the read). No Ember was used: Rooke's frames were "Feet only", and the bout used no contact technique.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-161-- Compression and Pressure were held. The forearm touch is costed in prose as the doctrine's price.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-162-- The Wind ceiling stays six on the sprung oak (about five on the second floor's boards). The landing beat is unshortened; the back-foot trial is logged as "a trial, not a gain".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-163-- New learned technique, not a fragment: **the heel correction against the second-year entry**, about one in three, then two in three, with the plain-entry mix still unsolved. Plus reading Ephram's shoulder drop. Both are skill, not capability.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-164-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-165-**Knowledge.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:166:- **Cael** knows the Standard's architecture (marks, strikes, par thirty, the bands, weighting, exhibitions rated for the figure only). He has priced Lira, Brom and Ephram correctly ahead of the panel. He knows the abbreviation on the card and that some unseen hand let the advisory go through; he does not know Vastin wrote it. He saw Karis mark a page in Rooke's manual (he does not know which), and he saw her write a note in the founding articles (he does not know what).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-167-- **Karis** has the third schedule and the exhibition provisions; the note (contents unknown to anyone); and the marked page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-168-- **Seln** said one sentence at the counter. Nothing was passed between them, and nothing was said of the B4 slip. "Thank you for the form." / "Mm." weekly.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:169:- **Vastin** knows the advisory, the routing slip's unknown initials, and that the roster stands. He has no knowledge of fragments and no suspicion of Seln.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-170-- **Rooke** has come as near as he ever has to asking, and has not asked.
