editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-914-- **Cael** knows the continental format; the Concourse's floors, sockets and ring size ("fifty-odd feet, a little longer one way than the other"); the draw (Zerin, Marek, Ivenne); Daeva's first read (no aim; inventory of Halcenvane's block); and Umber's want ("He wants the number to be right"). He has two Silver filings, with Rooke's council on each. He knows the trial rule and Karis's *Again.* He knows seat twelve is held, unplated and guarded; he cannot assign it and knows nothing of who it is for. Rooke has told him "don't try to sell him anything" about Umber, and has asked nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-915-- **Karis:** the trial rule beside the fielding clause, banked ("Until then it sleeps"); a note "for after Norhold"; Ivenne on her quarterfinal row; she has not said the name aloud. She logs the watchers as *All of them.* She has filed the coast stride for Ephram.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-916-- **Lira:** "Early"; Zerin's line; that sound can stand in for sight on an honest floor.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-917-- **Brom:** Marek first seed; that a door can be kept "moving"; "the wall".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-918-- **Ephram:** that two points can buy a man's reset; the coast coach's nod; that he likes calling better than winning, some days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-919-- **Rooke:** has read the trial rule (his thumbprint on the board glass, by Karis's account) and, she predicts, will put Cael fifth on the sheet without comment.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-920-- **Withrow:** "at least one of them is honest" (the duelist's filing kept under correspondence by Bracken).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-921-- **Seln:** has logged the road and the draw. He knows the filings and the panel. No reason is stated, and he knows nothing of the mechanism.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:922:- **Vastin:** seat twelve held at his own grade, unrequested by his office (one day-book line); he declined to think further. Nothing of fragments or Seln.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-923-- **Havel:** the seating order and the held instruction; he knows the grade and writes nothing. Four entries, eighty-six blank pages.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-924-- **Umber:** the seals whole; one judge struck for a quarter-point Blade drift on effect.
