editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1035-**Coordinator rulings and r1 changes (override the author's end-state below):**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:1036:- CALENDAR (OWNER-DECISIONS #41 default; BOOK_MAP §6 [M6-redated]): the west tower defers the exhibition ring by a notice on T5; the Copper final clears the main floor T9 morning; the ring is raised the night of T10, complete at dawn T11. Rooke's "four days … seven" is dead and is not restated. M7 onward: Shield captain T11; duelist and Vastin's seat T14 (chair held thirteen days — Seln's "nine" becomes "thirteen"); rest day/birthday T15; team trial T16; filing T19; convening T20; third place T21; finals T24; closing T26.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1037-- The fair-day veteran (ch36) is the M1/M2 buried fair-day Copper (she); her house "came up through its own region on her back".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1038-- #39 bouts as on the page: Lira–Zerin 4–9 in four; Brom–Marek 1–3 / 3–2 / 3–1 / 3–0 = 10–6 in four (E3's last Marek touch is an unflagged glance; 7–6 after three); Karis–Ivenne 10–9 in five; Brom SF 8–3; Karis SF 5–9; Lira QF 10–3; Ephram's exit 6–11. Brom is continental Copper champion.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1039-- Lira's burst shoulder is her LEFT: one burst over her rate of three in the Zerin bout (the diagonal cut on foot); a week of half work from T9.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1040-- Figures: Zerin 29 (a Silver figure; Silver assessment pending on her sheet); Brom and Marek level at 25; Karis SF 23 against 27.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1041-- Ternhall's lattice (PROVISIONAL house doctrine): three anchors are planted footholds that drain an ignition's heat into the floor; unanchored contact burns back into the palm. Ember stays contact-only; distinct from B4's Lattice Path.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1042-- Brom's registry tier on Ilsev's form is "Copper." with NO rank (BOOK_MAP: Copper formal).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1043-- Velmere letter: Brom reads it alone; he recites the line to Cael on the landing; no sender; the map's ten words exactly.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1044-- Rooke offered to scratch Karis before her semifinal and she refused; Rooke's clause on why her hands may fight when Lira's shoulder may not.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1178-- **The ring night:** the crews draw the plugs and set posts with a level and wedges. A woman oils each plug; Cael remembers the steward's grandmother.
