editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1384-- **Withrow:** "A filing with an argument stapled to it is a filing that thinks it will lose." "It's a list." The west tower's night clerk under the colonnade.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1385-- **Umber:** watched the ring come down at dawn; the trial office's two senior clerks and his deputy; "every figure was one we built a room for, after he'd arrived in it"; "a sheet that was already built to hold him".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1386-- **Bracken:** "Last night I slept like a quarry stone… That's twice this sitting. I may be getting used to it." He sits at their table.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1387-- **Ilsev's form (flag):** ten columns, each headed with name, house and registry classification. Her standing note *Authorizing office: not traced.* Her pen stopped mid-line at the E2 bell.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1388-- **Daeva** looks at the floor, not the fighters, at the presentation, longest at the barrier. The lane has a crack like a whip at its head, a struck-flint smell and a pale flicker; it makes ears pop and hair stand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1389-- **Rooke's review sheet** (the five findings, verbatim in ch46): *Ready. Not early.* · *Left the gap. Should have left it sooner.* · *A frame with a door in it.* / *She came from where no ramp was. Think about that.* · *South.* · *The diagonal. I had it on paper this morning and didn't know what it was.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1390-- **Ephram's speech** was "mostly" written on the road to the mill town and shown to Lira "at the waystation" ("a good speech with a sermon stuck on the end").
