editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1398-- Calendar per #41: T17–T18 the empty board; T19 filing (match line painted *filed; acceptance pending*); T20 convening (*Accepted.*); T21 third place, ring rebuilt at midnight; T22 the ring two days out; T23 the eve and the minute; T24 finals day (M9).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1399-- Rhagen lost its semifinal to the river academy off the page (one line given). THIRD PLACE (T21): Halcenvane beat Rhagen 3–1 in four exchanges under the M7 trial format (BOOK_MAP §8's three was a sketch); no unit figure posted; Withrow's protected line holds on the standings arithmetic. Standings: "Third of fourteen, as the count stands at the close of the trials. To be confirmed at the closing."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1400-- FINALS DAY'S CARD: the three bracket finals (Iron, Silver, Gold) and the team-trial final (Auremont v the river academy) on the morning card, then the match.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1401-- THE RING (canon; full spec in the M9 packet coordinator note): fifty-two by forty-eight; a half-inch dome off the oak round to a dry grounding trench every way (the long way north–south is the longest road downhill); four masts grounded twice into the trench; specification from Auremont's risk office. Daeva told Cael what the masts are rated to, at the west mast (ch52).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1402-- Daeva's own Storm vocabulary (asking, leaning, the road, the crooked lane, the air let go slack) stays hers in M9. Kindled at thirteen; six years since the garden court, seven in the program. She does not theorize what Cael is.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1403-- The keeper is "he" (edition ch28, ch42; the packet's "her" overridden). No weekday names: the calibration is the program's design session.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:1404:- Vastin left his office two mornings after the notice and resolved to stay for the figure; the later papers carried no routing slip and no initials.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1405-- Seln's slip at the fifth bell T23; the stove's ash already broken; nobody named. Seln and Ephram outside the council; Shadow sealed for the debt; Seln never told why.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1406-- The bank, as minuted on T23 in Hesk's book (see M9 packet note).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1407-- Bodies at T24: Brom's LEFT shoulder sore; Karis's palms pink; Lira's left arm held close only from habit; Cael's dull hold behind the eyes from deep recall.
