editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1425-**Every bout and figure in the movement.** No bouts were fought by Cael. Third place, Halcenvane against Rhagen (T21): E1 Rhagen (by a handful of quarter-minutes); E2 Halcenvane (by more than E1 went to Rhagen); E3 Halcenvane; E4 Halcenvane. **3–1 on exchanges; the objective ledger to Halcenvane "by a long way", the engagement ledger "by a little".** No unit figures are posted. The standings reading: "Third of fourteen, as the count stands at the close of the trials. To be confirmed at the closing."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1426-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1427-**Burst ledger.** Cael spent no burst in the trial; he ran it on reads and documented rates ("spent nothing he did not have to"). Lira spent one burst flat along the bank in E2 (the third lesson); others were not counted on the page.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1435-**Fragments and progression.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1436-- Six confirmed plus the anomaly ("one still place, untouched, in its own three words"). No new capability.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1437-- No public-record change; the bank is unspent until the flags of T24.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1438-- **Reading the medium** is trained to Lira scale, reliably: ten in ten in a shut hall, a half-beat early, off the air with her weight "put down". He also caught a squall's front early, twice, with the powder wharf's masts humming. The price shows only as narrowing (two incidents). He does not know the Gold-scale price.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1439-- **The bank is chosen spent**, minuted before the fact: Wind past six; the Ardenmere push at a fighting load past "four blows a sitting" (first load since the circuit record); Reydan's give on a scored floor (first since the bout at Ardenmere, its only paper); Ember past the two-contact public rule; the read to its depth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1440-- **Shadow sealed.** The year-old three-rule minute is restated in one line ("Nothing made to happen. Only inside a fight somebody else begins. The cost on paper first.").
