editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1708-**Prose vs plan differences.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1709-- (a) **Gates.** Cael's gate is north, Daeva's south (Gault's station at the north break, ch53). The five's rail is above the north break. The panel's long table is on the west side; the Compact row is over the east rail.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1710-- (b) **Her change.** She opens E1 at the wall, not the oak, paying ch52's "I'll have changed it by the day after tomorrow". She takes the oak in E4, satisfying §8's "she owns the middle".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1711-- (c) **The E3 strike is not a touch** (four flags of nine), so E3 can continue as §8 requires. At stoppage the flags stand one to nought for Cael. See owner flag 2.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1712-- (d) **Ember stays contact-only.** Its E4 failure is "nothing to touch": she sends fire down her lanes and stops walking them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:1713:- (e) **Vastin "leaving"** the row after the match is him going to the in-camera room under the observation right, so M8's "this time he would stay" holds. Cael misreads it ("Before the figure. Again.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1714-- (f) **The meeting** is in the timekeepers' office in the east tower (the note names it neutral ground). Brom sits on the step under the tower arch rather than standing at an arch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1715-- (g) **Hesk's reply** reaches the column on road day 11, written off the broadsides before Cael's letter arrived. It stays verbatim; the packet placed it with the letters.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1716-- (h) **The second pole** is written at nightfall on T25, after the meeting ("Tonight" in the protected text).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1717-- (i) **Ephram's correction** is about the lock-keeper's verses ("Eleven"), not the third-place trial.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-1718-- (j) **The optional Norhold session (C8) is not drafted.** Placing it was the owner's call, and the two days at Norhold after the match hold a destabilized fighter.
