editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-25-*Ephram: captain again from tomorrow, of the whole cohort this time. He has spent the recess learning the names of every first-year on the intake list, in order, so that he can pretend not to know them.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-26-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-27-He stopped there and looked down into the court for a while. A first-year was dragging a trunk across the flags on its corner, too proud to ask for help. Then he went on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-28-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-29-*The coats at the bottom of the hill: two at the ferry landing, two at the foot of the road, changing on the bell. Same arrangement as last year. Different men. The two I knew from the bridge never came back up the valley. These are older and stand differently, and they don't watch the gate the way men watch a gate they're learning. They watch it the way you watch a kettle you already know will boil.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-30-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md:31:*Vastin said there would be a sitting after the houses went home. The houses went home two months ago. Nothing has come up the road. I don't know whether that's good news or slow news.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-32-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-33-*What I carry, at the year's open: seven confirmed, the seventh Daeva's storm, and the quiet thing from the stair among them, sealed. Under all seven, the still place I don't count. The storm still has its flag on it. Nine of ten, this last week, the Wind came when I called and nothing else came instead. Nine isn't ten.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-34-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md-35-*Seventeen. Enrolled on a lawful basis. Third on the continent, with an entry no instrument could finish. Open the year.*
