editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-25.md-17-"She thanked him," said a woman in the front row, to nobody, astonished. She had a baby asleep on her shoulder and had been on her feet for Lira's second exchange. "Did you hear that? She gave him his whole grade and thanked him."
