editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-25.md-19-The man beside her said nothing. Neither did anybody else in the four rows round the house's bench. They sat with it the way you sit with a coin somebody has handed you in a currency you do not recognise.
