editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-25.md:21:The officer bowed again and turned and walked back the way he had come, the whole length of the north benches, at the same pace. Cael counted that walk, since he had missed the first. Fifty-one seconds, from the house's bench to the street door.
