editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-27.md-157-Bracken came in at the hall's side door with a sheet in his hand and his pen behind his ear. He had been at his counter since the riders left. He did not sit; he never sat in that room when there were enrollees in it.
