editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-27.md-237-He was not tired. Cael saw that as soon as he had asked. Seln's two hands were on the table, flat, one on each side of the fair copy of the order, close to the paper but not touching it, and his eyes were on the paper, and they had been on it, Cael understood now, since the moment he sat down.
