editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-15.md-99-That was all she said about it, and Withrow seemed to need no more. Cael did. He worked it out for himself on the stair later. The seat's clerks ate their noon meal on sitting weeks at the long low inn on the wharf, where he had once seen three of them at a window table with their collars undone; and they were clerks, and they talked about their day. The answer to the Archmarshal had been a joke at an inn before it was a letter on the Archmarshal's desk.
