editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-23.md-47-Rooke stopped walking. He stood by the trough with the waystation's one lamp behind him, so that Cael could not see his face, only the shape of his shoulders and his breath going up.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-23.md-48-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-23.md:49:"The registry doesn't read my book," he said. "It doesn't read the Stone's card, or what Withrow says at the gate, or what I think of her. It reads meet records. Stewards' sheets, sealed by a hall, filed with a district. That's all it's ever read about a fighter it hasn't got round to classifying yet." He took one hand out of his pocket and made a small flat shape in the air, like a man laying a sheet on a table. "Tomorrow there'll be a line on a confluence sheet with her name on it, and a Silver's name, and a figure. In a year or two some clerk at a counter in Ostrand will pull her file for the advancement sitting, and that line will be in it, in a steward's hand, under a hall's seal. And nobody can take it out again."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-23.md-50-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-23.md-51-He put the hand back in his pocket.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-23.md-52-
