editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-109-Nobody asked. That had been the arrangement since the recess, and it held. Lira tied her bundle with a knot she did not usually use. Karis opened her volume again at the page she had just closed. Cael watched Brom's hand come away from the pocket and settle on the board, and then, a moment later, go back to the pocket and rest flat on the cloth over it, and stay there, as if the letter might get out.
