editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-121-Karis had gone up before the piles were tied. When Cael followed her to the reading room at the ninth bell, she was writing, and he read what she was writing upside down before he knew what it answered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-122-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-123-*Research standing: enrolled, renewed in the recess by the council of the house in two sittings, entered as* Research, enrolled, standing. *Budget line: the house's accounts, the registrar's entry of the thirty-fifth day. Renewing officer: the Chancellor.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-124-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md:125:It was an answer, then. Only afterward did he see the question, printed on the other side of the sheet she was writing on. It was a form from the district fee office at Ostrand, which put its seal on every request a chartered house sent to an archive outside its own district. Her request of the thirty-fifth day, to Greyvane, for the founders' signature leaves, was in order and its fee was paid; before the office would seal it on, it asked the requester to state her standing, its last renewal, and the officer who had renewed it. It cited the section that let it ask.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-126-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-127-She finished, and blotted it, and did not say anything about it, and he did not ask.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-128-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-129-The door from the landing opened, and the assistant stood there in her cloak with her face pale round the mouth and red at the cheekbones.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-130-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-131-"I was boring," she said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-132-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-133-Karis put down her pen. "Shut the door. Come in. Start at the end."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-134-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-135-The girl shut the door. "At the end she said *thank you* in a very small voice and went away. Before that she kept looking at the stair." She swallowed. "Before that, I'd told her about the ninety-one. And the paragraph numbers. And that the next sitting's on the Fifth-day, and that the petitioner's conceded the provision is valid and doesn't allege fraud, and that the Compact's own inspection looked at the provision and it stood." She was going backward through it as Karis had told her to, and her voice steadied as she went. "And at the start I told her he's enrolled under a lawful provision, adjudicated at Greyvane on the public record, under seal, with the grant and two renewals on paper. Because she asked me what the enrollee was *really* like. A Mire girl from the north stair, on the covered walk, after supper. I hardly know her." She stopped. "That was the beginning."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-136-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-137-"Then you weren't boring," said Karis. "You told the truth quickly, to a question you weren't ready for, to somebody who came for gossip and got the code. That's the whole work; the rest is decoration. Do it like that for a year, every time anyone asks, and you'll be more use to this house than any clerk on the hill."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md-138-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-16.md:139:The girl stood very still. Then she said "Yes," very quietly, exactly as Karis said it, and went out, and they heard her sit down at the outer table, though there was nothing on it for her to do at that hour.
