editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-58.md-251-He stood up, and said a word of thanks to the room. He said it to the shelves and the table and the clocks, the way a man pays a small account on his way out of an inn. Then he went to the door, and out, and Cael heard his steps going down round the inside of the tower at the same even pace all the way to the bottom. He was going back down into a machine he knew to the last screw and could no longer account for.
