editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/EVENT-LIST.md-86-2. Noon refectory: the rumor in three versions; the open seat at the third-years' table by the west windows; Rooke sits in it and eats a whole meal and talks about hips; Ephram next; then the rest.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/EVENT-LIST.md-87-3. Gault on the covered walk [P] "I have written that down." It steadies Cael more than anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/EVENT-LIST.md-88-4. The notebook: the first Anchor page (own words; hypothesis; two tests; a shape and no numbers; the gap marked) [P] *Query for Seln: what Path holds people?*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/EVENT-LIST.md:89:5. Records hall, evening, Bracken's copy on the long table. Seln: Anchor Path; rare; nobody's champion; the service takes them early; enforcement; [P] "Whoever wrote that paper is done assessing." Karis draws the distinction once (Ternhall's anchors — planted footholds that drink heat; the Lattice Path — lines you can't see; this — a Path that holds people). Seln on her grade. Karis with Bracken's glass on the seal; the query to the district seat will come back paper all the way down; [P] the faceless layer has learned to write paper; the *yet*. Lira: what does it do when the paper doesn't work? No answer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/EVENT-LIST.md-90-6. The Crown yard after dark: Brom: "Show me." Cael, Brom and Seln (Seln comes unasked). Porter's chalk on the oak; the court drawn at size; the exits; Brom stands on her flag; Seln walks each line out and back; the long wall throws their voices back so they talk low. They learn where they'd have to go and that every way crosses her; they don't learn how far she reaches. Seln: leave the blank where you can see it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/EVENT-LIST.md-91-7. Back in the hall: the copy where they left it; Seln sits and lays his hands flat on either side of it and looks longer than anyone; he has stopped turning his cup. Close [P] "Whatever we're going to do, the schedule isn't ours anymore."
--
