editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md-38-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md-39-## Chapter 30 — The Upper Ferry (~5,300)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md-40-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md:41:1. **Havel, day 80–81, Ostrand** (cutaway). A clerk from the district seat at the inn by the bridge on the Third-day with a letter and a pencil rubbing: the Halcenvane registrar's inquiry, sent across "for the registers" because it concerns the proceedings and the district's records room is short. His thumb aches. Three checks over two days, each in its own room: the district's impression book (wafers pasted in by issue); the registry's printed schedule of seals of office (the engraved plates, this year's revision); the die number in the rim's beading against the strong-room copy of the cutters' issue ledger. The facilities office is on the register of offices — constituted this year by an instrument filed under seal. The seal on that instrument is the rubbing's seal. In none of the three. He drafts the usual reply: the office constituted on such a date by instrument filed under seal; inquiries to the issuing authority. The form has no line for what he found. At the inn: the five sheets, the sixth written — *a seal absent from every registry of seals* — fact only, by the rule of the sheets. He sees the first sheet's mark with no office and the sixth's seal with no register side by side and makes nothing of it. He stops; there will be no seventh, because a note of what the registers could not answer is only worth keeping while the registers answer everything else. He goes to bed with the river loud under the window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md-42-2. **Cael, day 82, before light.** The coach down the bluff road in the dark; the coats at the road's foot see it turn west; the near-bank road in mud; Brom with the record cases on his knees; Karis rehearsing the attestation under her breath; Lira asleep against the window; Seln on the bench with his eyes shut. Wind getting up, the rain gone east.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md-43-3. **The upper ferry.** First light at the narrows: a chain ferry between rock banks; the river loud and brown and narrow and deep. The ferryman (unnamed): crosses in any water because the narrows has no width to throw him; talks to the chain. "Road's good your side. Cut's dry. Only stretch that ever is." Chalk. On the far landing Seln gets down: he will walk the river path below the road and meet them at the milestone past the cut; a man on foot on a bank is a fisherman. Nobody asks. Cael notes it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md-44-4. **The cut.** The road climbs from the landing up a chalk spur; a cutting 440 yards long, the north bank twenty feet, the south bank lower and, at the middle, undercut by old floods into a hollow under the lip; twenty-four feet of cambered road with a ditch on the north side; at the east end a stream comes down a gully and goes under the road by a culvert with a stone parapet, and beside it the milestone. A skein of geese over, high. Dry chalk, white dust. A carter's cart across the east end by the culvert, a wheel off, nobody at it. The driver stops forty yards short.
--
