editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3525-   246	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r1.stdout.log:3526:   247	At Norhold, in a lent room of the timekeepers' office with forty clocks going on its walls, the Archmarshal had told Cael that the people who wanted this to stop would not go on using official channels much longer. This morning something that was neither one kind of channel nor the other had come up the bluff road in plain grey, politely, with real paper in its hand, and knocked. It had measured the door and gone away. There were other gates on the continent, and most of them had no Withrow standing in them.
