editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial-prompt.md-241-He looked for the provision. There was none. His petition had stood on two, the old one and the new, and the answer stood on nothing. That was the whole of its meaning. The seat had not ruled against him, because a ruling could be appealed. It had simply declined to hold a ruling at all, and there is no appeal from an empty room.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial-prompt.md-242-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial-prompt.md:243:*Fully constituted.* He tried the words for weight. A seat he had not been asked to sit on had been full before he asked. Very likely it had been full before the first sitting, before the wool exchange's floor was waxed for it. Whoever had drawn the schedule had known what the evaluation would find, and had known that the one officer who had put an instrument to the subject might find something else, and had drawn the schedule with no room in it for something else.
