editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial-prompt.md:1388:"And then nothing at all." Seln took his finger back. "You won't find this part in any code. No office has ever needed it written down. A finished inventory isn't an instrument. Nobody serves it. Nobody publishes it. It has no title. It is five files in five drawers in five offices, every one of them lawful, every one as dull as a laundry list, and all five indexed under one name." He squared the four beans again with the side of his finger, and did not touch the fifth. "If the seat rules for the house, the five drawers are never opened together. In time each office weeds its old papers, as offices do, and not one person anywhere will have broken a single rule. If the seat rules the other way, it takes one clerk one afternoon to fetch the five files to one desk. Then every gate shuts on the same morning. And the enrollee finds out what that sixth week was for on a morning when there is nothing left to do about it."
