editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-08.md-76-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-08.md-77-He had watched them build barges on the slip below Ostrand bridge. He had stood on the bank on the house's free afternoons for whole hours, because the work had an order in it and he liked orders. The shipwrights did not start with the sides you could see. They laid one long timber down the middle of the slip first, end to end, and squared it, and pinned it, and nothing else went on until it was true. Then the ribs went up from it on both sides, and everything that came after hung from the ribs. A barge could lose a plank and float. If the keel was wrong, nothing you nailed to it afterward would keep the river out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-08.md-78-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-08.md:79:"Everything else hangs from this," said Karis. "Every argument in the answer comes back to one fact: a seat has already heard this question and settled it on the public record, and the paper we're answering doesn't say otherwise. It doesn't even try. So the first thing on the table is the place where the question was settled." She put her palm on the transcript and left it there. "And then I don't move it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-08.md-80-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-08.md-81-She uncapped her pen and drew a sheet toward her, to write the heading.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-08.md-82-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/EVENT-LIST.md-57-- Rooke's invoice at the rail, standing: five against the book's three; her whole day's budget on boards in one bout; landing leg, hip; two days at half work, no frames. Cheap today; dear on a road with three bouts in four days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/EVENT-LIST.md-58-- The third-year at the rail with his kit: how long has she had the four-count? Since the second week; at speed since the sixth. Why not open with it? To learn whether his course sets on his count every time or only when he leads. "Every time." He takes it away to fix.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/EVENT-LIST.md-59-- Lira to Cael at the rail, collar dark, tapes off: the old pride; "I'm better now. I can admit I want it." Karis on the walk back: she used *admit*; enter it in the permanent section of the notebook, not the working pages. Cael writes it at the rail where Lira can see; she lets him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/EVENT-LIST.md:60:- Brom's envelopes, the same week. First: at Bracken's counter, the district seat's confirmation of the docket — the panel constituted, the season's record entered — and at the foot *outcome anticipated: advancement, per title*. Bracken reads *anticipated* aloud: a district never writes that; somebody decided ink was cheaper than pretending. Brom folds it into the left inside pocket.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/EVENT-LIST.md-61-- Second: the evening post, Velmere's wax. Up to his room. Two days on the small table beside the docket, squared together; the lamp moved off them. Lira reports it at supper as logistics; she went past the door twice a day (the stair), not in. "I'd like that noted. Not on paper." Her rule: when he opens it, nobody asks. Karis: she wasn't going to ask; she'd sit where he could tell her; learned it from him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/EVENT-LIST.md-62-- Third evening he opens it alone. He comes down to supper. "The face of a man being offered his whole ledger back." Cael files it, does not ask. Margin note: the number and the family in one fortnight; Brom has said "Noted" to neither.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair/EVENT-LIST.md-63-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-160-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-161-It was registry-seat stock, heavy and white, and the seal on it had been pressed into the paper rather than inked. That was a grade of reply in itself. A seat that inked its seals was writing to a colleague; a seat that pressed them was writing for the file. He weighed the grade before he let himself see a single word. Then he read the two sentences.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-162-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md:163:*The proceedings' evaluation seat is fully constituted. Supplementary findings are not contemplated by the schedule.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-164-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-165-He stood at the window with it a long time. The porter had gone in. The court was empty. He read it again, and a third time, and on the third pass something shifted, the way the figure in a puzzle-picture shifts and will not shift back. Until then he had been hearing an answer. Now he was looking at workmanship. And he knew the writer's school, because it was his own.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-166-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-176-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-177-He looked for the provision. There was none. His petition had stood on two, the old one and the new, and the answer stood on nothing. That was the whole of its meaning. The seat had not ruled against him, because a ruling could be appealed. It had simply declined to hold a ruling at all, and there is no appeal from an empty room.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-178-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md:179:*Fully constituted.* He tried the words for weight. A seat he had not been asked to sit on had been full before he asked. Very likely it had been full before the first sitting, before the wool exchange's floor was waxed for it. Whoever had drawn the schedule had known what the evaluation would find, and had known that the one officer who had put an instrument to the subject might find something else, and had drawn the schedule with no room in it for something else.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-180-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-181-And it had cost its writer nothing. He was too honest an instrument not to read that too. Two lines on good paper, nothing in them to answer, nobody behind them to be answered. It would have taken less time to write than to sand. It was exactly as good as his own had always been.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-14.md-182-
--
