editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log-1731-- **27:203** Lira silent all evening → asks the next thing → nobody answers → **written: she writes *WHAT DO THEY TRY NEXT, WHEN PAPER WON'T DO IT?* in her book and leaves it open, question up, between the rubbing and the copy; it is still there at the close.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log-1732-- **27:269** Seln reads something behind the paper (lamp image) → **interpretation removed; only the hands, the eyes on the order, longer than anyone, and the cup.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:1733:- **27:273** Vastin's warning → today the unofficial channel knocked → measured door → will knock without Withrow → **Brom, to the floor: "Fifty-one minutes… that clock room at Norhold. And you came out of it with one sentence for us." — the sentence given verbatim (BOOK_MAP §1); the "other gates" coda dropped.**
