editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log-3117-   147	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:3118:   148	Karis had the order's copy in front of her and was reading the seal's impression with a glass — she had borrowed Bracken's; the registrar owned three — and she said, without looking up, "The seal's format is registry. The office is unverifiable. Bracken's query to the district seat will come back in a week and it will say the office was constituted recently, correctly, by an instrument signed under a seal that is also a format and also unverifiable, and the trail will be paper the whole way down and there will be no person in it anywhere." She set the glass down. "The faceless layer has learned to write paper. That's what today was. They tested whether their paper works on us. It doesn't — yet. So they've learned that too."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log-3119-   149	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log-3120-   150	"Say the *yet*," said Brom.
