editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log-3133-   163	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log-3134-   164	*A man looking at a piece of genuine registry stock from an office that does not exist, in a hand he has not commented on, with a face that has stopped being furniture. The rest of us are reading the paper. He's reading something behind it, and whatever it is, he's been reading it for fifteen years, and tonight it moved.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log-3135-   165	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:3136:   166	*Vastin said the people who want this to stop wouldn't use official channels much longer. Today the unofficial channel knocked at the gate, politely, in genuine paper. It'll knock once more somewhere without a Withrow in front of it. Whatever we're going to do, the schedule isn't ours anymore.*
