editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/review-editorial.md-522-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/review-editorial.md-523-- **ch9:3–7.** "The fire-watch's oil book got a second line in its history". The book logs every lamp after the tenth bell by building (M1 ch6:3; B4 ch32:11 has the library's line as *second hour* every night). Say "its second line in Bracken's hand" or "on the registrar's authority". The same applies to "Two lines in thirteen years".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/review-editorial.md-524-- **ch12:95.** "like a tide coming up a beach" → "like water coming up a beach". Tide is a reserved Path name, and this is an audio book.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/review-editorial.md:525:- **ch12:225.** The confirmation's "*The panel is constituted*". See §4.3 item 1 (the ninety days).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/review-editorial.md-526-- **ch12:243–265.** The Velmere letter came on day 31. "Two days later it was still on his table", "one more night" and "On the third evening he opened it" can be heard as the 34th. Lira's leg is still up on Rooke's stool at that supper, which is days 31–32. "The next evening" for "Two days later" lands the opening on the 33rd, as the author's ledger has it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/review-editorial.md-527-- **ch11:99, ch12:173, ch13:247.** The meet countdowns (six weeks at ~day 26; five at day 30; four at day 42) put the meet at day 68, 65 and 70. "Not four weeks away now" at ch13:247 would bring them nearer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/review-editorial.md-528-- **ch11:47.** "on the morning I signed your roster" is the source's "on a roster" residue. Book 5's tournament roster is a real referent, so say "the morning I signed the tournament roster with your name on it", or change the image.
