editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1467-5. Karis writes it in her front matter. On the steps: the counsel to Karis about the price; Karis on what frightens her — he answered because the answer was obvious to him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1468-6. Evening: the house's counsel up the hill with them to work the produced record; stays in the guest room.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1469-7. **Day 76, the gate.** Way in: the lodge-man doing a thing he has never done (shutting the lodge window on the road and coming out without his hat); the boy runs. Cael from the wall stair to the gatehouse gallery above the arch — a stretch of walk with a waist-high parapet behind the bell-frame. The court's geometry (exits: the arch, the lodge door, the covered walk's arch, the lane round the lecture range, the stable passage — the only one with no door). Four riders, no livery, good horses.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log:1470:8. Withrow arrives with the counsel; follows the lodge's posted board (registry instruments: the registrar, the hour noted). She requires it read aloud. The order [P, verbatim body] with a six-word heading naming him (*In the matter of Caelen Hesk-ward.*); eighty-one words, Cael counts. Bracken's minute and forty seconds on the seal; genuine stock, registry format, issuing office unknown to him in thirteen years of this counter; "a facilities office, newly constituted"; constitution instrument; effective on presentation by an issuing authority.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1471-   Interleaved: pass one (dismount, she stops three steps on — nothing), pass two (during Bracken: she's on the court's one level flag, over the capped well).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1472-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1473-## Ch27 — Measure the Door
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1476-2. Noon refectory: the rumor in three versions; the open seat at the third-years' table by the west windows; Rooke sits in it and eats a whole meal and talks about hips; Ephram next; then the rest.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1477-3. Gault on the covered walk [P] "I have written that down." It steadies Cael more than anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1478-4. The notebook: the first Anchor page (own words; hypothesis; two tests; a shape and no numbers; the gap marked) [P] *Query for Seln: what Path holds people?*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log:1479:5. Records hall, evening, Bracken's copy on the long table. Seln: Anchor Path; rare; nobody's champion; the service takes them early; enforcement; [P] "Whoever wrote that paper is done assessing." Karis draws the distinction once (Ternhall's anchors — planted footholds that drink heat; the Lattice Path — lines you can't see; this — a Path that holds people). Seln on her grade. Karis with Bracken's glass on the seal; the query to the district seat will come back paper all the way down; [P] the faceless layer has learned to write paper; the *yet*. Lira: what does it do when the paper doesn't work? No answer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1480-6. The Crown yard after dark: Brom: "Show me." Cael, Brom and Seln (Seln comes unasked). Porter's chalk on the oak; the court drawn at size; the exits; Brom stands on her flag; Seln walks each line out and back; the long wall throws their voices back so they talk low. They learn where they'd have to go and that every way crosses her; they don't learn how far she reaches. Seln: leave the blank where you can see it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1481-7. Back in the hall: the copy where they left it; Seln sits and lays his hands flat on either side of it and looks longer than anyone; he has stopped turning his cup. Close [P] "Whatever we're going to do, the schedule isn't ours anymore."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-1482-
--
