editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4727-- **Brom, Karis, Seln, Ephram:** fit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4728-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4729-**Knowledge.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log:4730:- **The circle:** the road east as Lira's sum (the last Arbiter station four days past Ostrand loaded, three light; stamps stop there; two carters go past, the third turns at it and won't say why); the coastal default and *fled*; forty days after the fourth sitting's close; the five offices' inventories closed (Seln); Jent's sentence on the record; the fossil provision's two paragraphs (the second kept unmentioned); the escort order whole; a "facilities office" nobody can place; **Anchor Path** as a name and a use (rare; service; enforcement; holds people) — **inferred only: no range, rate or cost**; the three-way distinction (Ternhall's anchors / the Lattice Path / Anchor Path).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4731-- **Cael:** the fourth rider as a shape with no numbers (placement; the level flags; the arch's full span; every exit past her; squared to the doorless passage; no tell at the remount; even her horse trained). Rooke's account of the program as paper that can't be rubbed off. Nothing about falsification, a sub-layer, a maker, [UNBOUND] or Tide. The returns' wording still unknown. Nothing of Havel's note.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4732-- **Seln:** has still **not** been told why Shadow was sealed and does not know a sealed thing exists (his window touches only the two slips, the coals, the season's figures and Norhold). The maintenance records' content is not stated anywhere. He knows the clerk's timing at the confluence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4733-- **Lira:** the Silver's advice ("go on your fifth"); the panel's figure under a hall's seal; the town's caution explained (licences). She has not said aloud that the road east has no Silver card.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4768-**Proceedings.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4769-- Production order (day 71, served at the confluence on the delegation): the house's evaluation-linked floor records for *Caelen Hesk-ward*, year to date, at the fourth sitting. Produced day 75 in the house's boards; receipted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4770-- **Fourth sitting (day 75):** the hearing provision invoked once; Karis entered as advocate of record; the interrogatory *What evidence, if any, would defeat the petition?*; Jent's answer minuted. Next sitting set down.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log:4771:- **Escort order (day 76):** *In the matter of Caelen Hesk-ward.* + the Tier B body; a "facilities office" newly constituted; declined pending verification; no written refusal demanded; logged. Bracken to write to the district seat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4772-- File designations unchanged.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4773-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4774-**Open threads.**
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4807-- **The hearing provision (flag — M8 hook):** *Of the seat's hearing, and who may be heard*; struck in pencil in the general index a century ago; never repealed; para 1 (one question through counsel, on the record) last used ~140 years ago in a river district over a mill-race; para 2 (the advocate of record heard at the close, by the seat's leave) no recorded use; the door-log title *Advocate of record for the respondent, under the hearing provision.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4808-- **The gate (flag):** the gatehouse walk over the arch with the old bell-frame; the outer court 50 × 70 feet, flagged, sloping to gutters, dead level round the capped farm well; five exits (the arch; the lodge door; the covered walk's corner into the quadrangle; the lane round the lecture range; the doorless stable passage); the arch twelve feet deep; the lodge board's four lines (*CARTS — ROUND BY THE LANE. CALLERS — SIGN AND WAIT. POST — THE BAG ON THE HOOK. ANYTHING SEALED — FETCH THE REGISTRAR.*); registry stock from two mills (Bracken: the south mill).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4809-- **The escort order's heading:** *In the matter of Caelen Hesk-ward.* (see flag 2).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log:4810:- **The riders:** the lead rider (forty or so, weathered); two others; the fourth, a woman (unnamed). A "facilities office… constituted this year, for the proceedings".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/source-tracking.stdout.log-4811-- **Anchor Path (flag, as said by Seln):** on posting rolls, not meet cards; rare at any station; the service writes to the family the week the station enters it; "It holds people." **No range, rate or cost.**
