editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/recheck-r2.stdout.log-3620-    48	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/recheck-r2.stdout.log:3621:    49	The first was the district seat's: the advancement review's formal docket confirmation, panel constituted, the last Fifth-day of term, the season record entered as evidence, a line at the foot Bracken read aloud at the counter with the satisfaction of a registrar adding one to a tally he had kept for thirty years — *outcome anticipated: advancement, per title.* "They've written *anticipated* on a docket," Bracken said. "The registry does not write *anticipated* on dockets. Somebody at the district seat has decided the ink is cheaper than the pretense." He handed it over. "Iron-tier, by the last Fifth-day. The plaque's ribbon can go on your collar now. Nobody will think it's presumption."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/recheck-r2.stdout.log-3622-    50	
