editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-235-| **14.1** | Opens after the petition is signed: the crooked press has bitten the seal in at a slant; *can a faint edge be challenged?* walks him backward through the morning (the slip, the minute, paragraph seven, *adopts*), then the daughter's *no* before the two files it belonged to. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-236-| **14.2** | The clerk's stopped pen is the trigger: Vastin chooses to give the route and no reason. The clerk's return with the slip (new: he has begun to watch). The four-for-four as a failed attempt to steady himself; the scene ends on the nine leaves and the twelfth question. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-237-| **14.3** | Opens on the copy already in *held* in the evening; the junior's hour backfilled; new: Vastin's memory of his own junior stair and *Write what the instrument says*. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:238:| **14.4** | Opens on the denial already lying on the nine leaves and Vastin unable to remember putting it there; works backward (pressed seal, the tread, the sentences); the letter-book test; new beats: what became of the assessor he once refused; the first sitting's minute (*to be called*) against *fully constituted* — five chairs filled in four days and none offered to him; **he starts a refusal of his own in the old form, strikes it, and rewrites it with a citation**. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-239-| **14.5** | Opens on the next morning's consumables ledger in the clerk's view (the candle; his one non-work sentence and its answer); Vastin checks the drawer and reads the tab; the finding's four claims given end-first; ends on the bare addressee line. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-240-| **15.2** | The assistant trying to give back the print she bought twice; Brom prices the market by paper before anyone reads a title; the titles come last; **no log gloss** (P2). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-241-| **15.3** | Speed is the engine: Cael's first question in Withrow's office is *When did he get this?* — "He hasn't." Then how the counsel heard; then Withrow's form thirty; new beat: *should the house tell him?* — the counsel: a letter from the respondent would taint his finding; the kindest thing is not to write. Karis's provisions, with a new line of her own about having thought of him only as the man whose words were borrowed. |
--
