editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-341-| 14:169 | his own sentences of that family; the letter-book comparison | carried by his own pen writing the formula in a refusal to a guild hall (not a station) and stopping |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-342-| 14:177 | no citation → not a ruling | carried by action only: he rewrites his refusal *with* a citation |
