editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log-5523-editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5428:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:5:Vastin noticed it from the desk at a quarter past the second bell, because the court below his window was the one thing in the Compact's house that had never once been late in nineteen years. The man came out of his lodge at last with the paper bag and an apology in his shoulders, as if the birds had lodged a complaint against him, and they came down off the ledges in a grey shower and walked about his boots while he scattered the crumbs in his half-circle, the same half-circle as always, until the morning was set right.
