editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-cold.stdout.log-1249-It was registry-seat stock, heavy and white, and the seal on it had been pressed into the paper rather than inked. That was a grade of reply in itself. A seat that inked its seals was writing to a colleague; a seat that pressed them was writing for the file. He weighed the grade before he let himself see a single word. Then he read the two sentences.
