editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1207-    16	4. He drafts a petition for standing: the senior evaluator who personally assessed the subject asks leave to submit a finding. Two provisions, both old; the older one from before the standardizing, which uses *shall receive*. He cites both; a petition on one leg deserves to fall. He sets out his history from memory: four supplementary findings in forty years, four granted, each received and weighed — one decisive against the petitioning district's own case, and the district wrote to thank him. He predicts: standing within days, a finding entered at the next sitting.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1208-    17	5. The clerk at the dispatch ledger hesitates at the routing column; Vastin supplies the route ("Registry seat, Ostrand. Proceedings. Institutional."). The clerk has never sent paper from this desk *toward* a proceeding. Vastin notes the hesitation and what it says.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1209-    18	6. Day 43: a junior evaluator from the northern district brings a hard file — a station's Kindling entry against a young practitioner whose shown work outruns it. They go through it for an hour; inside tolerance; growth faster than the station guessed; *continue observation*. The junior leaves comforted. Vastin keeps the copy on the blotter after, reads one line too many times, puts it in "held", takes it out, puts it back. No word for it; it is not yet a thing. [plant; unnamed]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:1210:    19	7. Day 45, the fourth morning: the clerk's tread on the stair is wrong — single steps from the bottom, no pause at the door. Seat courier, not the post. Impressed seal, not inked (a grade of reply). [P] *The proceedings' evaluation seat is fully constituted. Supplementary findings are not contemplated by the schedule.* He reads it standing, sits, reads it twice more; on the third he hears it as a sentence he could have written — he has written hundreds of its cousins, closing doors cleanly so the person outside has nothing to hold. Good craft; among his best. Now aimed at him. No provision cited. It cost its sender nothing. "Fully constituted" — a seat he was not asked to sit on was full before he asked. He puts the sheet in *held* — no; in the boy's file.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1211-    20	8. He writes the finding anyway that evening, in his own hand, the addressee line left empty. The building's lamp rule (the floor's lamps out at the sixth bell). The clerk's one sentence in nineteen years that is not about the work — his own question (I'll give him: whether the Archmarshal would like the window shut, the pigeons are loud — no: a question that touches the man: "Will you be going home tonight, sir?"). Candle fetched and entered on the consumables under Vastin's name. The finding: the standard protocol cannot measure this subject; its silence is the instrument's limit, not the subject's fault; a re-evaluation whose result is known in advance is a procedure dressed as an evaluation; the honest instrument available is the demonstration record. The hardest page: the instruments are not at fault — the same sentence he has defended all his life for frames, now for a boy. Last paragraph: the schedule's purpose unknown to him; an evaluation that starts from its conclusion evaluates the evaluator. Nine pages. Into his own drawer in the cabinet of shallow drawers, under a heading he never needed before: [P] *Pending a proceeding worth sending it to.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1212-    21	
