editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1266-    75	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1267-    76	1. First light, the coach down; the cases. Karis at the ferry: we'll win on the text; brace for winning feeling like winning. Lira: you said that last time. Karis: I'll say it every time; saying it keeps a finding from rotting into a hope. Brom's pocket; Seln with eyes shut; the counsel adding to her minute. Withrow ahead in her carriage.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:1268:    77	2. The wool exchange: the four steps; the lot numbers cut in the boards; Cael's seat over *seventeen* again (he's sat on it every time). The covers are off the five evaluation chairs. Ilsev in the middle chair, files squared at their unchanging angle, sharpening a pencil into a paper fold so no shavings fall. Empanelment read: the evaluation seat constituted, the district's senior evaluator presiding (own wording). Havel at the junior chair, not looking. The hood; the hands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1269-    78	3. The clerk reads Daeva's statement into the minute; the seal receives it; nobody rises; set aside, not contemplated. Cael hears the rhyme with Vastin's two sentences: credentials were never the coin; the ladder isn't what listens.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1270-    79	4. Jent, forty minutes, no papers in hand: concedes the enrollment's execution at once; the provision; the documentation (repeats his compliment for the minute and says not to soften it). Then four numbered points: (1) the integrity provisions protect the registry's confidence, their opening line read; (2) a practitioner no standard evaluation reads is one the registry cannot have evaluated confidence in — "by definition", defined once; (3) the demonstration provision describes, it doesn't evaluate — he begins "produces no record", stops, says that is too broad and false, asks the clerk to strike it, restates narrowly (a record of a different kind); (4) the discretion to compel re-evaluation is the registry's and needs no defect. Asks the seat to find the question cognizable. Cites Umber's file by page. Sits. Cael: courteous, honest, unhateable; a good instrument used well; the file to open isn't his.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-1271-    80	5. The counsel, small and grey with her steel rule, rises and argues in four signposted movements: the text (three reconstructions, the directive's transitional schedule lists what it cancels and the clause isn't there); the precedent (Greyvane and the four rulings); the integrity provisions (she reads their preamble aloud — ninety seconds nobody in the room has heard; the ninety-one: eighty-four about things, seven about persons and all seven about conduct, none about what a person is). The seal's one question: incapable in law, or never so applied? "The second, and the second is enough" — own wording; Jent rises: he accepts a minute entry that it is novel; she repeats it to the gallery. Fourth: the demonstration record as evaluation — the grant and two renewals on paper, a season under a rating instrument, a tournament, the Compact's own inspection that declined to find; twenty-two officers who assessed him, named one by one into the minute, four minutes, silence. Karis's two cards: a struck page number; *the fifth point isn't needed* — not taken. Closing (own words).
--
