editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2566-   160	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2567-   161	It was registry-seat stock, heavy and white, and the seal on it had been pressed into the paper rather than inked. That was a grade of reply in itself. A seat that inked its seals was writing to a colleague; a seat that pressed them was writing for the file. He weighed the grade before he let himself see a single word. Then he read the two sentences.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2568-   162	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:2569:   163	*The proceedings' evaluation seat is fully constituted. Supplementary findings are not contemplated by the schedule.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2570-   164	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2571-   165	He stood at the window with it a long time. The porter had gone in. The court was empty. He read it again, and a third time, and on the third pass something shifted, the way the figure in a puzzle-picture shifts and will not shift back. Until then he had been hearing an answer. Now he was looking at workmanship. And he knew the writer's school, because it was his own.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2572-   166	
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2582-   176	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2583-   177	He looked for the provision. There was none. His petition had stood on two, the old one and the new, and the answer stood on nothing. That was the whole of its meaning. The seat had not ruled against him, because a ruling could be appealed. It had simply declined to hold a ruling at all, and there is no appeal from an empty room.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2584-   178	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:2585:   179	*Fully constituted.* He tried the words for weight. A seat he had not been asked to sit on had been full before he asked. Very likely it had been full before the first sitting, before the wool exchange's floor was waxed for it. Whoever had drawn the schedule had known what the evaluation would find, and had known that the one officer who had put an instrument to the subject might find something else, and had drawn the schedule with no room in it for something else.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2586-   180	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2587-   181	And it had cost its writer nothing. He was too honest an instrument not to read that too. Two lines on good paper, nothing in them to answer, nobody behind them to be answered. It would have taken less time to write than to sand. It was exactly as good as his own had always been.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2588-   182	
