editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2887-   160	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2888-   161	It was registry-seat stock, heavy and white, and the seal on it had been pressed into the paper rather than inked. That was a grade of reply in itself. A seat that inked its seals was writing to a colleague; a seat that pressed them was writing for the file. He weighed the grade before he let himself see a single word. Then he read the two sentences.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2889-   162	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:2890:   163	*The proceedings' evaluation seat is fully constituted. Supplementary findings are not contemplated by the schedule.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2891-   164	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2892-   165	He stood at the window with it a long time. The porter had gone in. The court was empty. He read it again, and a third time, and on the third pass something shifted, the way the figure in a puzzle-picture shifts and will not shift back. Until then he had been hearing an answer. Now he was looking at workmanship. And he knew the writer's school, because it was his own.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2893-   166	
