editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4341-   112	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4342-   113	"Walking them for what?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4343-   114	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:4344:   115	"So that the gate can shut on every field the same morning." Seln laid one fingertip beside each bean in turn as he spoke, not touching any of them. "Chapter fourteen lets the registry restrict an unclassified person: his standing, his papers, his endorsements, everything that's tied to him. A restriction that runs office by office leaks. Somebody hears, somebody moves a deed, somebody's cousin carries a letter across a district line before the freeze arrives. So before anything runs, a clerk goes round every fence the man has. Who sponsors him. Which houses hold his papers. What his people own, and where they own it. The tin box under the bench." His voice did not change at all on that. "Every gate is found and counted first. Then on the morning it's wanted, every gate shuts at once."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4345-   116	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4346-   117	"Before the ruling," said Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4347-   118	
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4357-   128	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4358-   129	"And then?" said Karis at last.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4359-   130	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:4360:   131	"And then nothing at all." Seln took his finger back. "You won't find this part in any code. No office has ever needed it written down. A finished inventory isn't an instrument. Nobody serves it. Nobody publishes it. It has no title. It is five files in five drawers in five offices, every one of them lawful, every one as dull as a laundry list, and all five indexed under one name." He squared the four beans again with the side of his finger, and did not touch the fifth. "If the seat rules for the house, the five drawers are never opened together. In time each office weeds its old papers, as offices do, and not one person anywhere will have broken a single rule. If the seat rules the other way, it takes one clerk one afternoon to fetch the five files to one desk. Then every gate shuts on the same morning. And the enrollee finds out what that sixth week was for on a morning when there is nothing left to do about it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4361-   132	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4362-   133	He folded his hands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4363-   134	
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4484-    32	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4485-    33	Senior evaluator of record, in the registry's grey, files squared on the seat's lap-desk at angles that had not varied by a degree since the first counter she had ever read his case across — the woman who had read that case at the counter of his life and had been, in every recorded act since, exactly correct. She had come in with the working morning's traffic rather than with the officers, carrying her own files, and had set them down and squared them, and had spent the four minutes before the opening reading the topmost one with the specific attention of a person who has read it three times already and intends to read it a fourth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4486-    34	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:4487:    35	Empaneled. The clerk read the empanelment into the minute: *the evaluation seat constituted, the district's senior evaluator presiding, scope per the code's institutional provisions.* Ilsev inclined her head to the seal at the exact depth the registry taught, and opened the first of her files, and the room proceeded, and Cael sat with the reading the sight of her produced, which was not comfort and was not its opposite.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4488-    36	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4489-    37	*The most honest instrument the Compact owns,* the log would say that night, *installed in a machine that is counting on her honesty to legitimize it. They didn't put her there despite her scruples. They put her there because of them. A seat that nobody can accuse of leaning is the only seat that can carry a corridor without the corridor showing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4490-    38	
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4744-   112	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4745-   113	The clerk rose and read the empanelment.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4746-   114	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:4747:   115	*Evaluation seat: constituted. Presiding: the district's senior evaluator. Scope: as the institutional sections of the code provide.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4748-   116	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4749-   117	Ilsev closed the fold of paper over the shavings, put it in her coat pocket, and bent her head toward the platform to the depth the registry taught, no more and no less. Then she opened the topmost file and began to read it with the patience of somebody who has read it three times and intends one more before she is asked a single question.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-4750-   118	
