editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log-2440-    59	He read it standing, which he did not do, and then he sat down, which he did not need to, and the office was very quiet, and he held the sheet at the reading distance his eyes now required and read it a second time, and a third, and the third reading was the one that mattered, because on the third reading he stopped reading it as a reply and started reading it as a *sentence*.
