editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r2.stdout.log-3388-+"He hasn't," said the counsel. "The seat answered him this morning, at Ostrand. His petition went to the seat by courier yesterday: standing to put a finding before it, signed and sealed as his own. The answer went out this morning by seat courier. Wherever the Archmarshal keeps his desk, it's a long road from the river. He'll have it tomorrow at the soonest." Her bag stayed in her hand. "We have it tonight."
