editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3772-    55	It came in the morning file, in the registry's flawless prose, on registry-seat stock with the seal impressed rather than inked — which was itself a grade of reply, and he catalogued the grade before he read the words. Two sentences.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3773-    56	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:3774:    57	*The proceedings' evaluation seat is fully constituted. Supplementary findings are not contemplated by the schedule.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3775-    58	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3776-    59	He read it standing, which he did not do, and then he sat down, which he did not need to, and the office was very quiet, and he held the sheet at the reading distance his eyes now required and read it a second time, and a third, and the third reading was the one that mattered, because on the third reading he stopped reading it as a reply and started reading it as a *sentence*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3777-    60	
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3779-    62	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3780-    63	He had written that sentence. Not that one — its sisters. A hundred of them, across thirty years, in the correct register, to the correct offices, declining unhelpful input: a field assessor's supplementary opinion not contemplated by the review's terms; a station's petition to reopen a closed finding not contemplated by the schedule; a junior officer's escalation not contemplated by the reporting structure. He had written them as a craftsman writes — cleanly, without cruelty, in the exact language that closed a door while leaving the person on the other side of it nothing to grip. It was good technique. It was among the best he had. And he recognized it now, at the reading distance his eyes required, from the receiving end, with the specific vertigo of a man who has spent his life fitting instruments and has just been handed one of his own, calibrated, pointed at him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3781-    64	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:3782:    65	The proceedings did not want the best evaluation available. He turned the sentence over, and it did not change. The proceedings had constituted an evaluation seat, and the seat was *full*, and the Compact's senior evaluator — the one officer who had put the instrument to the evaluand and written down what it returned — was not contemplated by the schedule, because the schedule had been written by people who already knew what the evaluation would find, and an evaluator who might find something else was not an asset to a schedule. He was an irregularity. The proceedings wanted the evaluation they had been built to produce. His grade, his thirty years, his personal assessment of the subject: not contemplated.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3783-    66	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3784-    67	He noted, with the evaluator's habit of keeping the instrument honest even while it recorded its own reading, that the sentence had cost the sender nothing. Two lines. Flawless. Deniable at every altitude. Exactly as his own had been.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-3785-    68	
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-4206-    32	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-4207-    33	Senior evaluator of record, in the registry's grey, files squared on the seat's lap-desk at angles that had not varied by a degree since the first counter she had ever read his case across — the woman who had read that case at the counter of his life and had been, in every recorded act since, exactly correct. She had come in with the working morning's traffic rather than with the officers, carrying her own files, and had set them down and squared them, and had spent the four minutes before the opening reading the topmost one with the specific attention of a person who has read it three times already and intends to read it a fourth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-4208-    34	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:4209:    35	Empaneled. The clerk read the empanelment into the minute: *the evaluation seat constituted, the district's senior evaluator presiding, scope per the code's institutional provisions.* Ilsev inclined her head to the seal at the exact depth the registry taught, and opened the first of her files, and the room proceeded, and Cael sat with the reading the sight of her produced, which was not comfort and was not its opposite.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-4210-    36	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-4211-    37	*The most honest instrument the Compact owns,* the log would say that night, *installed in a machine that is counting on her honesty to legitimize it. They didn't put her there despite her scruples. They put her there because of them. A seat that nobody can accuse of leaning is the only seat that can carry a corridor without the corridor showing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-4212-    38	
--
