editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-9879-    62	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-9880-    63	He had written that sentence. Not that one — its sisters. A hundred of them, across thirty years, in the correct register, to the correct offices, declining unhelpful input: a field assessor's supplementary opinion not contemplated by the review's terms; a station's petition to reopen a closed finding not contemplated by the schedule; a junior officer's escalation not contemplated by the reporting structure. He had written them as a craftsman writes — cleanly, without cruelty, in the exact language that closed a door while leaving the person on the other side of it nothing to grip. It was good technique. It was among the best he had. And he recognized it now, at the reading distance his eyes required, from the receiving end, with the specific vertigo of a man who has spent his life fitting instruments and has just been handed one of his own, calibrated, pointed at him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-9881-    64	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9882:    65	The proceedings did not want the best evaluation available. He turned the sentence over, and it did not change. The proceedings had constituted an evaluation seat, and the seat was *full*, and the Compact's senior evaluator — the one officer who had put the instrument to the evaluand and written down what it returned — was not contemplated by the schedule, because the schedule had been written by people who already knew what the evaluation would find, and an evaluator who might find something else was not an asset to a schedule. He was an irregularity. The proceedings wanted the evaluation they had been built to produce. His grade, his thirty years, his personal assessment of the subject: not contemplated.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-9883-    66	
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-9884-    67	He noted, with the evaluator's habit of keeping the instrument honest even while it recorded its own reading, that the sentence had cost the sender nothing. Two lines. Flawless. Deniable at every altitude. Exactly as his own had been.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log-9885-    68	
