editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-662-- **The visitors' log (flag):** the program clerk's second ledger from shortly after the first sitting; twenty-six names in a fortnight; four from outside houses (two Rhagen, the lake house, a northern house).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-663-- **Wing three's gallery (flag):** a narrow timber gallery over the west door from when wing three was the house's examination room, used to store benches until the porters cleared it for the four observers; observers enter by the lodge book.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-664-- **The Current third-year (flag — style):** Iron Rank Four, tall, glides "the way water goes over a weir"; two glides and a bend; adapts to straight glides, then glide-and-step.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-665-- **Cael's small burst (flag):** a burst spent short and low so that from above it reads as a quick step; learned this year, written only in the rotation's private margins. Consistent with the band; no new rate.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-666-- **The fee office (flag):** the district fee office at Ostrand seals every chartered house's request to an archive outside its district; it may query the requester's standing (a cited section); its query to Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-667-- **The Ternhall archive keeper (flag):** an unnamed woman Karis has known since her first year; her private four-line letter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:668:- **The lodge (flag):** the lodge-man (grey beard, bad knee, kept the gate since before Bracken); the wing may read the arrivals book on the Seventh-day; **the road column**, a line every bell since "the year of the thieves", on the order of the chancellor before last; the carter and the gatepost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-669-- **The post room (flag):** behind the records hall's counter; the post porter (twenty years at the sort) has a strapped left shoulder; Seln does the sort.
