editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-728-- **Karis:** the coastal letter ("It was true"); the induction; "Memory improves things"; the card; *Advocate* true for a day; "He wasn't even careful"; the three-way distinction; "how little of it there was".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-729-- **Seln:** one correction; two looks; the lamp at the dairy step; the clerk's timing ("I'd have gone at the same touch"); Anchor Path; came unasked to the Crown yard; "A blank you can see is worth something"; his hands flat, cup unturned.
