editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:16:| 21 | The Landing | 4,414 | 5 | **LIRA cutaway (~1,970).** Way in: the second carter's "You buying a wagon or selling one?" Her rule from the floor — never the same corner twice; three errands that are real; the grey coats look past her (insulted, then glad). Carter one (day 58, mules): manifests stamped at every station, then a gap at the paper's edge; "nobody with a book". Carter two (day 61, a woman with good horses and a Mire daughter): fords, four days loaded / three light, the bad well; "Nobody's got a book to write you in." Carter three (day 64, young, a new wagon): exactly where the last station stands — "I turn there." The sum at the second switchback; the meet card re-chalked eight days later (the confluence's repairs); the ladder; her oath to leave rooms on her own feet, and the next room one she loves. The note. **Cael, day 66:** the board; Seln at the copying table — "Five drawers. Full. Shut." (the seals change color). Lira on the north wall at dusk: "Fifth-day"; the meet put back; "Does it cost you much? The band." / "Like a toll." **Day 68, the small room** (an old dairy, slate shelves, a joiner's table that leaves as firewood): Brom with the good chair — "It's for the council." Lira: "Why do we keep answering them?" — the carters as a sum; the third "Turns round at it." **Karis** stands and reads the second paragraph of a coastal default ruling first (the respondent's own letter quoted as proof); *fled*; her other column (Norhold's clause, Bracken's book, Greyvane, Vell's ledger; Denvash with nothing written); Brom: "Was it wrong?" "It was true." "The machine has a form for leaving." **Seln's one correction**: forty days after the fourth sitting's close; the code counts days, not sittings. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:17:| 22 | Both Roads | 4,790 | 5 | Brom tips the chair: **"Prepare both roads." "Win the sittings. Keep a box."** — Lira counts three. The word *box* stays. Shirts, all the strapping, the plaque ("If I leave it, you'll go back for it"); hand to the LEFT pocket; **"It's the second box that's the problem."** — the sealed letter, twenty-three days; nobody asks. **Cael's first pole at full strength**, from the bottom: Pellin as a woman with a brass plate, eleven seconds, fourteen; forward through Vell, Greyvane, the grant and two renewals on paper, the inspection, Norhold's clause, Umber's *no number goes here*; "People change with the weather. Text doesn't." **"I'm not leaving the room while the text still works."** He pre-empts the objection; "always Karis who read it." **Karis names it an induction** (a run; "Every rule anybody ever broke looked exactly like this the evening before"; a tally, not a guarantee). **Lira: Fenmark's perfect form; "It's not ground. It's a floor."**; joists somebody laid; *Both roads* — it costs Cael nothing and nobody makes him pay. Seln's two looks. The slow spirit kettle; Karis: "Memory improves things"; **"It was the night we asked."** Seln lights them up the dairy step and crosses to the wing. Log. **SELN cutaway (~2,330), the dark wing**: no lamp, the fire-watch's square on the counter; his one correction examined (forty days as a narrow door); fifteen years, nineteen postings, sixty-three subjects, the followed few; the maintenance records copied twelve years ago on his fourth posting, understood in a green corridor between two appointments — *whose question it had been*; the boy inferred (the mill-town table; two slips burned on the coals; a season that never settled; Norhold spent on purpose); his own true, empty reports filed with the boy's receipts; the brass key held and returned; the dairy step and the lamp he held for each of them; ***The deciding has stopped being quiet.*** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:18:| 23 | Colors | 4,322 | 5 | Day 69 dawn: the colors out of their cedar trunk, the creased pennant; Bracken's travel sheet ("Attendance. Again."). Day 67 flashback: Bracken's question; **Withrow's one sentence** ("The house sends its fighters in its own colors, Registrar, or it does not send them, and nobody at Ostrand has yet asked me to stop sending them."). The road north: Karis changing one word on a card four times (not shown to Cael); Seln without his case; **Rooke at the waystation trough** — the registry reads meet records; "The program is getting things written down where nobody can rub them off"; Cael hears his own pole in it, and every rung on this side of the stamps. The confluence (callback to B5): the innkeeper's framed ruling; Withrow's tea and "careful in writing for sixty days". **The card**: one line on the non-qualifying year's lighter card; Rooke's filing under the host's exhibition provision (stated once); the Silver's acceptance on a barge manifest, *Yes. Glad to.*; Silver eleven years, never asked by an Iron. The river apron at night: Lira frightened "of being a good loss"; "Watch my feet." **Rooke's brief** in bread: courses under courses; four counts — "Before four it's a promise. After four it's a floor."; lose the first slowly, one burst; the second is the exam; the Stone: "Watch his knees." Lira: "growth". **Dawn**: Rooke walks the floor (slower: the stewards' letter said *repairs*); Cael charts **no light, no rebound, a quiet side that pulls**, leaves a fourth line blank (the south-west corner under sawdust). Breakfast: Brom's bowl; **"He calls it honesty. I'm going to call it the ropes."** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:19:| 24 | Two Touches to One | 4,445 | 5 | **Lira v the Silver Rank Eight** (Force, the confluence's bargemen), exhibition under the host's provision, five exchanges at most, two touches ends it. Seln in the loft; the Stone alone at the quiet east end; Cael watches only her feet. **E1 (his):** the hum under the boards; a course laid under the course; her one burst finds the bottom; he takes the centre by building; two small checks in the south-west; the fourth count knocks; the floor carries her into the north-west post — the new rope gives nothing; his palm. **E2 (hers):** the four-count lie; she lands her whole weight on his course at the count of two — a promise broken before it's kept; inside; the quiet east side used as a door; **her third burst**, palm to the ribs. **E3 (clean):** short settles; a fan of courses walks her south-west like a raft on a pole; the crossways planks seen at last (the flood repair); three-quarter purchase; out of a finished structure with bursts four and five, the fifth off rising boards; the fourth fact written. **E4 (his):** he stands on his kept courses and gives her no promises; the sixth burst, past the floor's five, half a stride short; **two to one on the fourth.** Panel 28 / 27. "Eleven years. Nobody asked." / "I asked." The Stone's hands over his head where the river academy's row can see. At the rope Cael tells her feet first, as promised; **Rooke writes the false quarter as his** (*The stewards wrote that they'd mended something… Mine.*); Lira's lesson in her own words ("It's the same bout, sooner"); "Yes."; **"Again. Faster. It's there."** read aloud; the bill (six against three; one borrowed; the post across both shoulder blades; the landing leg, two days at half work); "Still on your feet in the fourth." |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:20:| 25 | The Rail | 4,682 | 6 | Seln's head turns first; **the production order** — an officer in grey with a case held before him, the clerk carrying nothing; **fifty-one seconds** counted along the north benches, the hall turning from the Current girl's bout; *the complete records of evaluation-linked floor work of the enrollee of record, Caelen Hesk-ward*; Bracken reads it standing, signs, takes the duplicate; **Withrow thanks the officer by full grade** to four rows. Lawful in every line; "The hour is not in the order." **The hall's regard adjusting**: applause taken back to be weighed; the steward; two correspondents out. Lira at the rope: "They waited… Till I'd lost well"; the boy's card and his mother. Supper: **Seln's clerk** on the south benches since the first bell, out at the second touch, back with the officer nineteen minutes later; "They waited for the hall"; Withrow: bind the records "in the house's own boards… they may look at it handsomely." **LIRA cutaway (~1,770), day 72**: the corridor of trestles; the Silver — "go on your fifth"; "Because you'd asked"; the town and its licences; the finals' politeness. Evening rail: the steward's sheet *for your file*; the ladder counted rung by rung (Iron Rank One; 27 in the red book; one point under a hall's seal; the Stone; Zerin's *Silver bracket. Next cycle.*; the corridor); four nights since the dairy; no Silver card past the stamps. Cael with the order's duplicate. **"One of these is the best night of my life." / "Noted."** The folds won't lie the same way twice; it will go in the box. Home in rain; the watcher looks at the colors trunk; log: *They can't touch the paper. The paper's honest. So they choose the hour.* |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:21:| 26 | One Question | 4,770 | 5 | Flashback: **the assistant finds a struck heading** in the code's index — *Of the seat's hearing, and who may be heard*; para 1, a question through counsel; **para 2, the advocate heard at the close by the seat's leave** (no recorded use); a hundred and forty years; the counsel: "Old law is an old floor… one question… And the second paragraph we leave exactly where it is… Until the end." (M8 setup, light.) **Day 75:** the side-door officer enters Karis as *Advocate of record for the respondent, under the hearing provision*. Lot seventeen. **The records produced in the house's boards**; Jent: never seen a production order answered in boards. **The interrogatory**: the hood permits one question; the counsel speaks the card from memory; Ilsev looks up and stays up; not one pencil moves; Havel writes the time; **"None, Advocate. The petition doesn't turn on evidence. It turns on discretion."** Cael's dairy notes: every receipt is evidence — *He had brought receipts to a room that did not take them.* Steps: "Did you hear what he called me?"; the counsel: "Keep the other paragraph… In your pocket, not your mouth."; Jent: "A good question, Advocate. I'd have asked it myself, in your chair."; Karis: "He wasn't even careful." The card with question and answer goes inside her notebook's front cover. The counsel stays the night. **Day 76, the gate:** the lodge-man shuts his road window; the boy runs; Cael behind the old bell-frame on the gatehouse; the court (the level flags round the capped well); **pass one** (three paces, nothing). Withrow reads the lodge board (*ANYTHING SEALED — FETCH THE REGISTRAR*); "My lodge-man… has never once heard one read"; **the order read aloud**, 81 words with its heading *In the matter of Caelen Hesk-ward.*; **Bracken's minute and forty** (paper, deckle, glass, then his thumb on the impression with eyes shut); **pass two** (the one level patch); south-mill paper, registry die, an office he has never met in thirteen years; "Facilities"; "my book has a column for the office that issues… I can't write four riders in it." |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:22:| 27 | Measure the Door | 5,338 | 6 | **Withrow's refusal** (four reasons, a sentence each; the lodge-man's pencil). **Pass three** (the only feet of flagstone from which the whole arch lies open). **"Voluntarily"** pitched up at the gatehouse; Cael's hands; Withrow: "You are speaking to me, Officer… If your office wants something from a student of mine, it writes to me." **Pass four**: five chalk-lines in his head, all past her; squared to the doorless stable passage; nothing laid; the remount without the half beat. A fair copy and a pencil rubbing taken at the lodge; **no written refusal asked** (the counsel explains why); *Measure the door.* Withrow's log: "…said up at the gatehouse roof, and… there was nobody on the roof." **Noon**: the riders multiply in the queue; the one empty place at a full table; **Rooke eats in it** and talks about hips; Ephram, then the cohort. **Gault: "I have written that down."** — the one sentence he can stand on. **The notebook's first page for her**; a shape and no numbers; **"Query for Seln: what Path holds people?"** **Records hall:** Seln — **Anchor Path**; posting rolls, not meet cards; the service writes to the family; "It holds people"; **"Whoever wrote that paper is done assessing."**; "the best tool somebody owns." **Karis draws the distinction once** (Ternhall's anchors — her own footholds that drain heat; the Lattice Path — unseen lines; Anchor Path — holds a person). The rubbing; paper all the way down; **"The faceless layer has learned to write paper."**; "how little of it there was." Lira: "What's the next thing they try?" — no answer. **The Crown yard**: Cael, Brom and Seln (unasked) chalk the court at size on the oak; Brom on her flag; five lines all past him; the long wall doubles their voices; no reach known; Seln: "A blank you can see is worth something." **Back in the hall**: Seln's hands flat either side of the copy, his cup unturned, looking longer than anyone; **"Whatever we're going to do, the schedule isn't ours anymore."** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:24:## State at movement end (for the ledger)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:26:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names; feet and yards. Day 58 Second-day, day 61 Fifth-day, day 64 First-day: Lira's three carters. About day 57: the confluence's stewards put the road meet back eight days for repairs to their hall (from day 63 to day 71; see owner flag 1). Day 66 Third-day: the note; "five drawers… shut" (the last two days before). Day 67: Withrow's colors sentence. **Day 68 Fifth-day: the small room**; Seln in the dark wing that night. Day 69 Sixth-day: the delegation leaves (Withrow and Bracken in the hired carriage, the coach, the program wagon; Rooke, the Stone, Lira, the Current third-year, Karis, Seln, Brom, Cael; Ephram stays). Day 70: the confluence at dusk; the card; Rooke's brief. **Day 71 First-day: the exhibition (afternoon); the production order served a quarter past two.** Day 72: finals; the corridor; the last evening at the rail. Days 73–74: home in rain. **Day 75 Fifth-day: the fourth sitting** (records produced; the one question). **Day 76 Sixth-day, second bell: the escort order at the gate**; noon refectory; Gault; the notebook; records hall; the Crown yard after dark. Bracken writes to the district seat on day 77 (the answer due about a week later). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day. The *fled* default would enter forty days after the fourth sitting's close (day 75) — the code's count, said by Seln.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:31:- **Brom, Karis, Seln, Ephram:** fit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:34:- **The circle:** the road east as Lira's sum (the last Arbiter station four days past Ostrand loaded, three light; stamps stop there; two carters go past, the third turns at it and won't say why); the coastal default and *fled*; forty days after the fourth sitting's close; the five offices' inventories closed (Seln); Jent's sentence on the record; the fossil provision's two paragraphs (the second kept unmentioned); the escort order whole; a "facilities office" nobody can place; **Anchor Path** as a name and a use (rare; service; enforcement; holds people) — **inferred only: no range, rate or cost**; the three-way distinction (Ternhall's anchors / the Lattice Path / Anchor Path).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:36:- **Seln:** has still **not** been told why Shadow was sealed and does not know a sealed thing exists (his window touches only the two slips, the coals, the season's figures and Norhold). The maintenance records' content is not stated anywhere. He knows the clerk's timing at the confluence.
