editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:167:## Formula (formula_metrics.py, ch21–27, after the last edit)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:198:**Length.** 32,683 words (metrics; 32,761 by wc) against ~34,000 (≈96%). Each planned scene has its room (the dairy ~6.5k across ch21–22; Seln's window ~2.3k against ~3k; the bout ~3.4k against ~3.5k; the Crown-yard rebuild ~0.9k against ~1k). Added beyond the packet, each with a job: the north-wall scene (the band's cost asked aloud), Rooke at the waystation trough (the ladder as paper), the river apron ("Watch my feet"), Seln's supper reading of the clerk, the Silver in the corridor. Not padded. The book stays short (~8–9k under budget after four movements).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:202:**Development beats.** Cael ≈ 15 (≈5.6 per 10k of his ~26.6k words): the band named as a cost ("Like a toll"); the pole at full strength and Karis's induction landing like a touch; "both roads" costing him nothing — and the table letting him keep it; Rooke's paper ladder heard as his own pole; every rung on this side of the stamps; watching only her feet; sharing the missed corner; the hall's applause weighed and kept; "they choose the hour"; receipts brought to a room that does not take them; the name at the top read aloud in his own gate; the hands at "voluntarily"; Gault's board still nailed down; a shape and no numbers; the schedule not theirs. Supporting beats spread across Lira (6–7, two in her windows), Brom (3), Karis (4), Seln (3 + window), Withrow (3), Rooke (3), Bracken (2), the Stone, the counsel, Jent, Gault, Ephram, the assistant.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:204:**POV.** Cael ≈ 81.5%; cutaways ≈ 6,060 words (18.5% of M4): Lira 1,966 (ch21) + 1,767 (ch25); Seln 2,326 (ch22). Book share after four movements ≈ Havel 1.2k + Vastin 5.1k + Lira 3.7k + Seln 2.3k ≈ 12.3k of ~122k ≈ **10%** (plan 13%).
