editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:209:2. **The escort order's count and address (#44).** The Tier B body is 75 words and carries no name ("the enrollee of record therein named"). To honour #44 (*Caelen Hesk-ward* in instruments) without touching protected text, the order is read with a six-word heading, *In the matter of Caelen Hesk-ward.*, and Cael counts **eighty-one** "from the name to the hand". If the owner prefers the name inside the body (as M1's first page), the count needs re-squaring.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:210:3. **The hearing provision (M8 hook).** Two paragraphs; para 2 lets the advocate of record be heard at the close by the seat's leave (no recorded use). This is the BOOK_MAP §11 #4 default's "fossil provision", set up lightly and kept unmentioned at the seat. Karis is entered in the door log as *Advocate of record for the respondent, under the hearing provision* — please confirm before M7–M8 rely on it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:211:4. **Seln's window** carries his trade's counts (nineteen postings; sixty-three subjects; the fourth posting twelve years ago; the green corridor) and his own reports as "true among true things" in the same drawer as Cael's receipts. No Shadow, no sealed thing, no content of the records, no *falsification*. Check the plant's altitude before M6.
