+Brom may know it. The hour itself was arranged as unwritten and unwitnessed, but Book 5 `chapter-59.md:51–53` then has Cael tell the whole long table what was said “word for word, as near as he could get it,” while Karis writes it all down. Brom and Seln are present in that knowledge state; the Book 5 `AFTER MOVEMENT 9` ledger separately records Lira/Brom/Karis and Seln as knowing “the hour as told.” Brom's “Fifty-one minutes” also agrees with Book 5 `chapter-58.md:267–273`.
+
+### Seln's realization — PASS
+
+`chapter-22.md:133` stays at the M6 boundary: a return has an office-to-office route; beyond the last station there is no bag, clerk, or drawer. It names no Shadow, no sealed protected thing, and no content of the maintenance records. The sealed item in the cutaway is the ordinary weekly return. The lowercase “shadow” at `chapter-22.md:137` is literal shelf darkness, not the Path.
+
